# Cosmic muon run.
#
#   MuonSim -n 10000 -o cosmic.mac.root macro/cosmic_muon.mac
#   MuonSim -n 100 -s 12345 macro/cosmic_muon.mac      reproducible
#
# A focused macro: the full annotated reference is macro/run.mac, and the
# generator is documented in doc/generator.md.

/run/initialize

/run/verbose 1
/event/verbose 0
/tracking/verbose 0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What to save
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Muons, hadrons and ions, with their steps. Bits: 1 heavy, 2 non-shower e±,
# 4 gamma, 8 shower e±, 16 optical. A step needs its bit in BOTH masks.
#
# Gammas (bit 4) are left off deliberately -- they are 75% of the file and 95%
# of the tracks. Turn them on when the study is about them, not by default.

/ROOT/savetrackopt 1
/ROOT/savestepopt 1
/ROOT/savehitphoton 1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The generator
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Muons are launched on a virtual hemisphere, dome upwards, of radius R centred on
# the point given. R is the whole acceptance, and the cost goes as R^2, so it wants
# to enclose every detector volume and nothing more.
#
# Where the FLAT SIDE goes is a correctness question, not a tuning one. Launch
# points lie on the dome, so a muon is generated only if it enters the sphere
# through the upper half. For a steeply falling track that is automatic, but a
# near-horizontal one passing BELOW the centre enters through the lower half -- and
# is never generated. So anything sitting under the flat side has an acceptance hole
# for inclined muons.
#
# Hence the flat side sits at z = -460, the underside of the PSMD modules lying in
# the pit, which is the lowest detector surface in the apparatus:
#
#   0     - 400 - 60  =  -460
#   floor   gap    module thickness
#
# With every detector at or above that plane, any muon reaching any of them from
# above must cross the dome, whatever its inclination.
#
# R is then set by the farthest detector point, the top corner of the water tank:
#
#   tank top corner   (3205, 3205, 7692)  ->  9327   <-- binding
#   tank floor corner (3205, 3205, 4550)  ->  6756
#   PSMD wall, top    (1770, 1770, 3720)  ->  4872
#   PSMD floor module (1740, 1740, -460)  ->  2461
#
# R = 9500 mm clears it by 173 mm. The empty pit below -460 holds no detector and
# needs no covering.
#
# THE TANK HEIGHT SETS R. geo::frame::kTopZ is where the tank stands, so changing it
# moves the binding point and this radius has to be recomputed. A sphere left too
# small silently drops muons that should have been generated -- nothing warns.

/gen/vertex cosmic input /home/cupsoft/Works/AMoRE/Muons/MuonSim/data/muon_flux.root hemisphere 0 0 -460 9500 mm

# /gen/list

/run/beamOn {nevent}
